<title>UK: German private heating oil storage at 65 pct - trade.</title>
<headline>German private heating oil storage at 65 pct - trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German private household stocks of heating fuel stood at 65 percent capacity at the end of September, compared to a historical average of 71 percent, according to a German heating oil supplier.</p>
<p>The rate implies steady demand in the coming weeks and reflects reluctance on the part of buyers to enter the market at a time of high prices. &quot;There is quite a lot still to obtain ...but it's not easy to tell when to buy,&quot; the supplier said.</p>
<p>On average stock levels have been at 71 percent at the end of September in the period since 1991, the supplier said.</p>
<p>-- William Maclean, London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
